64-infinite-lists: infinite lists consumed lazily from Python.

Seam: a goal that takes a prefix of an infinite Curry list; Prelude.take
applied from Python to a Curry symbol that is an infinite list; a goal with
two free parameters narrowed over an infinite list; a Python iterator
crossing the boundary as a lazy list.
Sources: PAKCS 3.4.1 examples inflists.curry, First.curry (Michael Hanus,
BSD license); memo A2 (an iterator as a list); catalogue P3, P5.
Backends: py, cxx.  Oracle: oracle.out (PAKCS 3.4.1 on the same goals; the
iterator line is spelled as a finite list there).

Expected output: ten Fibonacci numbers, five primes, ten Hamming numbers;
take 15 fibs the fifteen Fibonacci numbers; First.goal1 [O, S O];
First.goal2 x y binds x to S O and y to O.  take 3 over itertools.count(10)
gives [10, 11, 12], and the next element of the iterator afterwards is 13:
only the three elements taken were drawn.  Pins no defect.
